# API-First CLI Contract

Treat this repository as the reviewed GraphQL operation producer.

- Keep `queryPayloads/*.txt` as SDK operation input. SDK must not consume CLI models, parsers, docs, tests, or site-location data.
- Make generation deterministic. Validate every generated operation against the fetched introspection schema.
- Keep payload regression tests in the existing GitHub Actions PR flow. Do not duplicate them in Jenkins schema automation.
- Keep GeoNames/site-location refresh independent from schema generation. Never include unrelated `siteLocation.db` or `siteLocation.json` churn in schema PRs.
- Fail generation on operation errors or artifact mismatches; never publish a partial generated tree.
- Preserve generator fixes for nested `accountId`, complex selections, and conflicting interface/union fields.

## SDK Handoff

- Trigger SDK generation from the exact 40-character CLI PR commit SHA, never a branch name.
- Pass the CLI PR URL with the SHA. If the CLI branch advances, regenerate from the new SHA.
- SDK merge/tag stays blocked until that exact commit reaches CLI `main`.
- Do not merge, tag, release, poll, or auto-fix downstream CI unless explicitly requested.

## Required Checks

- Run `python -m pytest tests/test_generated_graphql_payloads.py`.
- Confirm generated operation count and model/JSON/TXT parity.
- Confirm the worktree contains no unrelated live-data churn.
